{
  "_doc": "Example fallback chains for `rein providers` and `rein route prepare`. Copy to ~/.config/rein/fallback-chain.json (or set PIPELINE_FALLBACK) and edit providers, models and costs to your own accounts. Review chains should list strong models only. The fields effort, capabilities, context_tokens, billing and probe_bound are used only by automatic selection (`rein route auto`, docs/ROUTING_SELECTION_DESIGN.md): worker_chains[<policy>] then names the APPROVED candidate set (its order is ignored) and the union of review_chains the approved reviewers. billing.pool qualifies a quota by provider/account/plan/window and is shared by every provider drawing on it; billing.unit is its native unit (usd, kiro_credits, agy_credits, subscription_percent, tokens) and units are never merged. probe_bound is the owner-declared worst case of ONE availability probe in that unit: without it a provider is never probed. effort must be expressible on the launch command line (--effort, --variant or -c model_reasoning_effort=) or left out. The numbers below are placeholders: replace them with your own plan names and limits.",
